WEBVTT

00:00:07.583 --> 00:00:08.583
"As in the figure to the right, the crystalline structure"

00:00:08.583 --> 00:00:09.667
"known as a body-centered cubic unit consists of"

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:10.375
"known as a body-centered cubic unit consists of"
The math exam's final problem.

00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:11.708
"multiple cubes <i>a </i>having sides 1 arranged periodically,"
The math exam's final problem.

00:00:11.708 --> 00:00:12.500
"with an atom at each vertex and at each cube's center."
The math exam's final problem.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.792
"with an atom at each vertex and at each cube's center."
Half of our grade couldn't even make it this far.

00:00:13.792 --> 00:00:15.167
"Most alkaline metals, including Na and K,"
Half of our grade couldn't even make it this far.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.708
"are body-centered cubic units."
Half of our grade couldn't even make it this far.

00:00:16.708 --> 00:00:17.250
"are body-centered cubic units."
The other half arrived in the nick of time,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.917
"Focusing on atom A[0] in a body-centered cubic unit,"
The other half arrived in the nick of time,

00:00:18.917 --> 00:00:20.208
"of all the points within the space,"
The other half arrived in the nick of time,

00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:22.208
"the domain D[0] consists of the set of points closer to A[0]"
already lacking the energy needed to solve it all the way.

00:00:22.208 --> 00:00:24.375
"than to any other atom. Find the volume of D[0]."
already lacking the energy needed to solve it all the way.

00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:29.375
The only ones capable of getting
full marks in the time remaining...

00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:38.750
...were these two.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.167
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:58.000
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.417
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:06.083
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:08.792
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:01:08.792 --> 00:01:12.625
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:16.625
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:19.583
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:24.792
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:01:24.792 --> 00:01:30.375
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:35.792
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:01:35.792 --> 00:01:41.292
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:01:41.292 --> 00:01:43.917
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:46.583
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.375
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.000
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.708
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:01:54.708 --> 00:01:57.417
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.250
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:05.208
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:02:08.958 --> 00:02:12.958
"12th Period: Think Outside the Box Time"
"by Manami Okuda"

00:02:18.375 --> 00:02:22.500
What was it Nagisa always used to say?

00:02:23.333 --> 00:02:29.292
Aw... How can two fellow humans
have such a gap between them?

00:02:29.292 --> 00:02:32.458
I guess you've got
different talents, huh, Karma.

00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:35.125
Easy for you to say...

00:02:35.125 --> 00:02:40.458
If you ask me, I'm not sure
which of us is the real genius here.

00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:46.792
What we call "talent" is
the part of us that others can't see.

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:51.583
Like Sugino,
who can slide right in with people.

00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:56.875
Like Okuda, who can totally
lose herself in something she loves.

00:02:56.875 --> 00:03:01.667
Like Terasaka, who can act
without giving it a single thought.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:04.542
"My Plan (Secret)"
From where I stand, those are all talents.

00:03:04.542 --> 00:03:09.750
Everyone has this
talented domain that I can't see,

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.417
so in that sense, we're all the same.

00:03:13.417 --> 00:03:20.500
The issue here... is whether I can
see this problem with my own talent.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:25.083
Oh, man--I <i>definitely</i>
won't have enough time for this.

00:03:27.375 --> 00:03:31.292
Atoms, body-centered cubic units...

00:03:31.292 --> 00:03:34.792
I can't let these
unnecessary details throw me off.

00:03:34.792 --> 00:03:36.792
Once I get down to the essentials, it's simple:

00:03:36.792 --> 00:03:38.250
"the domain D[0] consists of the set of points closer to A[0]
than to any other atom. Find the volume of D[0]."

00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:42.250
Find the volume of your own domain

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:45.500
here in this box, surrounded by enemies.

00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:58.667
When both sides are evenly matched,

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.167
their attacks meet in the middle.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:06.250
So from there inward is my domain!

00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:17.333
Gotcha. You won't be sneaking
into my domain anytime soon.

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:21.208
Eight enemies surround
the inside of this cube.

00:04:21.208 --> 00:04:24.958
So if I find the volume of
the eight areas I've sealed off

00:04:24.958 --> 00:04:28.375
and subtract it from the cube, I'm left with...

00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:32.042
A[0]--my domain!

00:04:35.542 --> 00:04:39.833
Once I lock down this space,
I'll have the correct answer!

00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:49.500
Ruling over this space:
the perfect theme for me!

00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:55.292
A different kind of ruler--not like my father.

00:04:55.292 --> 00:04:58.750
Right now, he's obsessed with proving that

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.333
his own "rational education" is correct.

00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:06.917
It may break a person,
but it will not educate them.

00:05:06.917 --> 00:05:11.125
I'll set him straight and
give him a piece of my mind!

00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:13.292
To take control--

00:05:13.292 --> 00:05:17.042
<i>That </i>is my duty as a son!

00:05:18.333 --> 00:05:19.500
There it is!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.667
The volume of one of the
sealed-off areas is an aggregate

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:25.375
of one hexagonal
and three triangular pyramids!

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:37.958
"multiple cubes <i>a </i>having sides
1 arranged periodically"

00:05:38.833 --> 00:05:45.250
Hang on... This doesn't call
for any tough math at all!

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:48.833
It's separated out into this one little cube,

00:05:48.833 --> 00:05:52.042
but if this is an atomic crystal,

00:05:52.042 --> 00:05:57.083
there'll be more of the same
structure outside this cube, too.

00:05:57.083 --> 00:05:59.042
Which means...

00:05:59.042 --> 00:06:01.833
...the world doesn't end here!

00:06:03.417 --> 00:06:09.125
And from where I stand,
everyone has their own talent

00:06:09.125 --> 00:06:11.417
and their own domain,

00:06:11.417 --> 00:06:14.167
so everyone's the same...

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:21.083
All I could see from inside the box
was mere fragments of everyone.

00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:28.708
Just as I claim my own domain,
everyone else will claim theirs.

00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:33.042
We're all the same size,
the same distance apart.

00:06:33.042 --> 00:06:36.000
If we're all cut from the same box,

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.042
those eight contiguous boxes
can be broken up

00:06:38.042 --> 00:06:40.500
into the same proportion,

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:45.333
so each person's fragment
accounts for one-eighth.

00:06:45.333 --> 00:06:48.417
The box holds a whole me

00:06:48.417 --> 00:06:53.042
and one-eighth each
from eight people's fragments.

00:06:53.042 --> 00:06:56.417
In other words, inside this cube

00:06:56.417 --> 00:07:01.542
the ratio of me to the
other eight has got to be 1 to 1.

00:07:01.542 --> 00:07:04.542
And if it's 1 to 1 inside the box,

00:07:04.542 --> 00:07:10.667
the volume of the domain
I can claim is up to half the cube!

00:07:14.708 --> 00:07:18.792
Well, geez... This is primary-school stuff!

00:07:27.958 --> 00:07:34.875
No need for drawn-out
calculations or complex diagrams.

00:07:34.875 --> 00:07:39.500
If you just tweak to the fact that
there's a world outside yourself...

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.917
"Final Problem"
"Karma Akabane: 20/20 points"

00:07:42.833 --> 00:07:44.542
Time's up!

00:07:45.792 --> 00:07:48.417
Asano... the test is over.

00:07:48.417 --> 00:07:50.125
"(cube's volume) - 8"

00:07:50.542 --> 00:07:53.000
One more line...

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.208
Dammit--and I knew the answer, too!

00:07:56.458 --> 00:07:57.833
"Final Problem"
"Gakushu Asano: 17/20 points"

00:07:59.333 --> 00:08:03.542
And so the surging wave of our
end-of-term exams receded at last.

00:08:07.375 --> 00:08:09.125
Now then, class,

00:08:09.125 --> 00:08:12.750
I'll be returning your compiled exam papers.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:18.333
Did your second blades
manage to reach their targets?

00:08:20.625 --> 00:08:22.083
"Tentacle"

00:08:22.292 --> 00:08:26.208
No grumbling about
a point here or there, now.

00:08:26.208 --> 00:08:28.083
Were your scores this time

00:08:28.083 --> 00:08:32.583
good enough to get you
into the top fifty overall?

00:08:32.583 --> 00:08:37.458
The main campus will be posting
the overall ranks right about now,

00:08:37.458 --> 00:08:41.833
so let's start with
ranks here in the E Class, too.

00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:44.167
"Tentacle"

00:08:44.167 --> 00:08:47.625
"Second End-of-Term Exam: Top 50"

00:08:51.083 --> 00:08:54.042
"Second End-of-Term Exam: Top 50"

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.667
I-I--

00:08:56.667 --> 00:08:57.458
"44: Sosuke Sugaya" "46: Ryoma Terasaka"

00:08:57.458 --> 00:08:59.750
"44: Sosuke Sugaya" "46: Ryoma Terasaka"
I'm 46th?!

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:02.208
Isn't Terasaka dead last in the E Class?

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:05.375
If Terasaka came in 46th...

00:09:05.375 --> 00:09:07.375
...then that means...

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.792
We did it!

00:09:10.792 --> 00:09:11.083
"5: Kotaro Takebayashi" "6: Meg Kataoka"
We did it!

00:09:11.083 --> 00:09:12.417
"7: Yukiko Kanzaki" "8: Ren Sakakibara"
We pulled down the Big Five in the battle for top spot, too--

00:09:12.417 --> 00:09:13.542
"5: Kotaro Takebayashi" "6: Meg Kataoka"
We pulled down the Big Five in the battle for top spot, too--

00:09:13.542 --> 00:09:14.083
"5: Kotaro Takebayashi" "6: Meg Kataoka"
practically a perfect win!

00:09:14.083 --> 00:09:15.042
"3: Rio Nakamura" "4: Yuma Isogai"
practically a perfect win!

00:09:15.042 --> 00:09:15.750
"3: Rio Nakamura" "4: Yuma Isogai"
And first place is Karma for once!

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:16.750
"1: Karma Akabane" "2: Gakushu Asano"
And first place is Karma for once!

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.083
And first place is Karma for once!

00:09:19.083 --> 00:09:21.917
How does it feel, Karma,
to go after that first-place rank

00:09:21.917 --> 00:09:24.833
on such a high-level battleground... and win?

00:09:24.833 --> 00:09:28.042
Um, whatever, I guess.

00:09:28.042 --> 00:09:31.208
It seems your battle against
the perfection-boasting Asano

00:09:31.208 --> 00:09:35.250
came down to that final math problem.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:39.583
About that... I'm not sure exactly why,

00:09:39.583 --> 00:09:43.958
but I don't think I could've solved it
if I hadn't spent this year with you all.

00:09:43.958 --> 00:09:46.125
That's the kind of problem it was.

00:09:46.125 --> 00:09:49.000
It sure was a slog getting to
this point, though, huh?

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.125
Our most fervent wish--after a
successful assassination, anyway!

00:09:52.125 --> 00:09:55.208
We really did beat the A Class!

00:09:55.208 --> 00:09:57.458
We can go to our first-pick schools!

00:09:57.458 --> 00:09:59.333
Girls will be throwing themselves at us!

00:09:59.333 --> 00:10:00.917
Go, us!

00:10:00.917 --> 00:10:03.333
Yay! Girls everywhere!

00:10:03.333 --> 00:10:04.625
Feels like a final episode to me.

00:10:04.625 --> 00:10:07.042
Hey! It can't end yet!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.208
You feeling okay, Takebayashi?

00:10:10.208 --> 00:10:11.833
Yeah, it's just...

00:10:11.833 --> 00:10:15.500
So much happened since
I dropped down to the E Class,

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.083
but I'm glad I stayed.

00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:19.542
Aw, why so glum, chum?

00:10:19.542 --> 00:10:22.875
--'Sweird comin' from you! Ha ha ha!
--Yeah, leave the ugly mugs to Terasaka.

00:10:22.875 --> 00:10:23.667
Say what?!

00:10:23.667 --> 00:10:25.500
Terasaka, you're choking him!

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:25.917
"Tentacle"
Terasaka, you're choking him!

00:10:25.917 --> 00:10:26.958
"Tentacle"
Well?

00:10:26.958 --> 00:10:30.042
"Tentacle"
I think I can get into my dream school with this.

00:10:30.042 --> 00:10:32.708
"Tentacle"
For architecture, was it?

00:10:32.708 --> 00:10:37.083
Yeah. That's why I want a
high school that's big on the sciences.

00:10:37.083 --> 00:10:38.333
Hmm.

00:10:38.333 --> 00:10:43.375
Boy, those A-Class twerps must be
white as sheets right about now!

00:10:43.375 --> 00:10:46.667
I bet they never thought they'd lose to <i>us</i>!

00:10:46.667 --> 00:10:51.917
For their part, the A Class did well
on the first half of the exams.

00:10:51.917 --> 00:10:54.750
But it seems more and more
students got hung up

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:58.083
on the tougher problems
in the second batch of subjects.

00:10:58.083 --> 00:11:03.083
Well, sure. You can't keep
your bloodlust going for that long.

00:11:03.083 --> 00:11:05.708
Even with daily assassination training,

00:11:05.708 --> 00:11:09.583
it's rough staying in that
frame of mind for a whole day.

00:11:09.583 --> 00:11:14.083
If you want to dope with bloodlust,
cramming won't work.

00:11:14.083 --> 00:11:18.167
You have to nurture it
slowly but surely, over time.

00:11:18.167 --> 00:11:22.500
How? To lose--after all we went through?

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.458
With your studying, you <i>couldn't </i>win.

00:11:25.458 --> 00:11:27.292
That's all it comes down to...

00:11:27.292 --> 00:11:32.083
...although the scores I earned
are nothing to brag about, either.

00:11:32.083 --> 00:11:36.292
I'll make good use of this frustration,
that's for damn sure.

00:11:36.292 --> 00:11:38.833
Even in high school, I'll keep winning,

00:11:38.833 --> 00:11:42.208
and looking for ways to let you win as well.

00:11:42.208 --> 00:11:45.167
So, please...

00:11:45.167 --> 00:11:47.000
...lend me your support in turn.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.083
Asano...

00:11:48.083 --> 00:11:50.000
Asano...

00:11:51.667 --> 00:11:53.333
Can you still say that,

00:11:53.333 --> 00:11:58.500
now that the battle on which
you bet your life is over?

00:11:59.583 --> 00:12:02.333
Principal Asano, sir!

00:12:02.333 --> 00:12:05.542
Life is always a great unknown.

00:12:05.542 --> 00:12:09.667
Will losing a battle
mean losing your life as well?

00:12:09.667 --> 00:12:13.000
You never know until the battle's over.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:17.292
That's why you have all
needed to keep on winning.

00:12:17.292 --> 00:12:21.042
I have an obligation to teach you as much.

00:12:21.042 --> 00:12:25.333
I'll get your brains better
by graduation time, all right.

00:12:25.333 --> 00:12:27.667
Principal Asano?

00:12:27.667 --> 00:12:30.375
It's clear to us now.

00:12:30.375 --> 00:12:34.792
With these current methods,
we can't beat the E Class.

00:12:36.042 --> 00:12:40.417
The E Class and Asano here--
both grew stronger through defeat.

00:12:40.417 --> 00:12:45.792
Our strength is no match for
the flexible strength they have.

00:12:45.792 --> 00:12:49.625
We apologize for falling short of our goal.

00:12:49.625 --> 00:12:54.125
If you wish, you may
send us down to the E Class.

00:12:54.125 --> 00:12:58.542
I have the feeling we can learn
and grow more there.

00:13:00.333 --> 00:13:03.333
You have your answer, sir.

00:13:05.375 --> 00:13:06.958
Asano!

00:13:08.375 --> 00:13:09.792
Asano!

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:15.917
That look on your face--
like you're glitching out.

00:13:15.917 --> 00:13:20.250
I might just be seeing the
fatherly side of you at last.

00:13:22.833 --> 00:13:26.208
--I'm fine.
--If you'll excuse us, sir.

00:13:35.917 --> 00:13:39.917
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Karma Akabane"

00:13:42.125 --> 00:13:43.750
All right, students--

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:48.083
You've formally received your
qualifications to move out of the E Class.

00:13:48.083 --> 00:13:50.958
So is anyone looking to leave this mountain?

00:13:50.958 --> 00:13:52.833
Of course not!

00:13:52.833 --> 00:13:57.292
We found our second blades--
This is when it gets serious!

00:13:57.292 --> 00:14:01.208
What other environment
is this suited to an assassination?

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.208
Gluttons for punishment, eh?

00:14:05.208 --> 00:14:09.417
Then for your reward this time,
I'll tell you my weakn--

00:14:17.208 --> 00:14:19.167
The school building!

00:14:19.167 --> 00:14:21.875
Prepare to vacate the premises.

00:14:21.875 --> 00:14:23.292
Principal Asano!

00:14:23.292 --> 00:14:26.083
The Board made the decision this morning:

00:14:26.083 --> 00:14:29.917
We're tearing down
this old campus building today.

00:14:29.917 --> 00:14:33.000
I'll have you move to the
new campus of our affiliate school

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.292
opening next school year.

00:14:35.292 --> 00:14:39.500
Until graduation, you will help us
performance-test the building.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.000
A new campus?!

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:44.708
With a surveillance system
and an anti-escape system

00:14:44.708 --> 00:14:46.500
drawn from correctional facilities,

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:50.458
they can study in an environment
akin to a more civilized prison.

00:14:50.458 --> 00:14:55.542
The new E Class: the culmination
of my educational theories.

00:14:55.542 --> 00:14:57.708
B-But moving us <i>now</i>?

00:14:57.708 --> 00:15:01.125
No way! We wanna graduate
from <i>this </i>campus!

00:15:01.958 --> 00:15:05.667
You'll carry out your educational vision
to the very end, won't you.

00:15:05.667 --> 00:15:06.833
Indeed.

00:15:06.833 --> 00:15:12.667
But make no mistake:
<i>You </i>are no longer useful to my education.

00:15:12.667 --> 00:15:14.917
And this...

00:15:14.917 --> 00:15:15.333
This is where I kill you.

00:15:15.333 --> 00:15:17.375
"Notice of Dismissal"
This is where I kill you.

00:15:18.458 --> 00:15:21.083
K-Koro Sensei's walking papers?!

00:15:21.083 --> 00:15:25.458
He actually went there:
He played his forbidden ace in the hole!

00:15:25.667 --> 00:15:25.875
"Koro-Labor Union"

00:15:25.875 --> 00:15:26.333
"Koro-Labor Union" "Koro Sensei's Weak Point #31: Downsizing"

00:15:26.333 --> 00:15:27.750
"Koro-Labor Union" "Koro Sensei's Weak Point #31: Downsizing"
Th-That's wrongful dismissal!

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:31.167
It works hilariously well on this octopus.

00:15:31.167 --> 00:15:34.375
Can a super-creature even stage a protest?

00:15:34.375 --> 00:15:36.625
And so you won't jump to any conclusions,

00:15:36.625 --> 00:15:40.292
this is nothing but a tool to control my target.

00:15:40.292 --> 00:15:43.417
I have come, Koro Sensei,

00:15:43.417 --> 00:15:43.792
"Stop the Firings!" "And the salary's low, too!"
I have come, Koro Sensei,

00:15:43.792 --> 00:15:47.208
"Stop the Firings!" "And the salary's low, too!"
to kill you once and for all.

00:15:47.208 --> 00:15:52.042
You are... no longer necessary
for my education, you see.

00:15:52.042 --> 00:15:53.667
Are you serious?

00:15:53.667 --> 00:15:56.583
I know you're superhuman and all,

00:15:56.583 --> 00:16:01.458
but our octopus won't go down
quite as easily as you think.

00:16:01.458 --> 00:16:06.875
Hold off the demolition for now.
I have some work to do inside.

00:16:11.542 --> 00:16:13.917
Where'd that notice of dismissal come from?

00:16:13.917 --> 00:16:17.583
What could Principal Asano be thinking?

00:16:17.583 --> 00:16:19.667
Now, then, Koro Sensei...

00:16:19.667 --> 00:16:22.125
If you don't want to be fired,

00:16:22.125 --> 00:16:25.875
if you want to protect this classroom,

00:16:25.875 --> 00:16:28.458
I'll have you join me in a little gamble.

00:16:28.458 --> 00:16:30.250
A gamble?

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:35.125
I've prepared five subjects' worth of
test questions and five hand grenades.

00:16:35.125 --> 00:16:40.333
Four of them are anti-Sensei grenades;
one works on humans.

00:16:40.333 --> 00:16:43.083
They're the real deal.

00:16:43.083 --> 00:16:45.833
They are identical in appearance and smell,

00:16:45.833 --> 00:16:48.500
and made such that, once their pins are pulled,

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:51.708
they'll explode the moment their handles rise.

00:16:51.708 --> 00:16:53.292
I've pulled their pins

00:16:53.292 --> 00:16:56.625
and placed them carefully between
random pages in the test books,

00:16:56.625 --> 00:16:58.542
handles in place.

00:16:58.542 --> 00:17:03.292
You will open the book and
solve the problem at the top right.

00:17:03.292 --> 00:17:06.167
As soon as he opens it,
the handle will pop up and--

00:17:06.167 --> 00:17:10.417
Yes--he'll almost certainly
be hit with an explosion.

00:17:10.417 --> 00:17:14.417
But he can't move an inch
until he solves that problem.

00:17:14.417 --> 00:17:21.000
You'll handle the first four books,
while I'll take the last one.

00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:26.500
If you manage to kill me
or force me to withdraw,

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:30.708
I will permit you
and the E Class to remain here.

00:17:30.708 --> 00:17:34.333
Let's see... Ah, Terasaka.

00:17:34.333 --> 00:17:38.417
Use a formula to find
Koro Sensei's odds of winning.

00:17:39.667 --> 00:17:44.708
An anti-Sensei grenade explosion
won't kill <i>you</i>...

00:17:44.708 --> 00:17:44.875
"1st Book"

00:17:44.875 --> 00:17:46.083
"1st Book"
To do that, we'd need to save the real grenade till the end.

00:17:46.083 --> 00:17:47.375
"2nd Book"
To do that, we'd need to save the real grenade till the end.

00:17:47.375 --> 00:17:48.625
"3rd Book"
To do that, we'd need to save the real grenade till the end.

00:17:48.625 --> 00:17:49.667
"4th Book"
To do that, we'd need to save the real grenade till the end.

00:17:49.667 --> 00:17:50.875
"5th Book"
To do that, we'd need to save the real grenade till the end.

00:17:50.875 --> 00:17:59.000
4/5 times 3/4 times 2/3 times
1/2 equals 1/5. Twenty percent.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:00.417
Correct!

00:18:00.417 --> 00:18:05.042
But the octopus has to take
four deadly grenades in a row,

00:18:05.042 --> 00:18:08.792
and you can just safely
tap out soon as it gets ugly.

00:18:08.792 --> 00:18:11.000
This is ridiculously unfair!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.542
Terasaka...

00:18:13.542 --> 00:18:17.000
You'll find that the world
is just one injustice after another.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:20.417
Especially between the weak and the strong.

00:18:20.417 --> 00:18:25.417
That's why I've taught you
to be the strong ones.

00:18:25.417 --> 00:18:28.292
So will you give it a try?

00:18:28.292 --> 00:18:33.042
It's also a test of how serious you are
about your chosen profession.

00:18:33.042 --> 00:18:37.583
If I were you, I'd jump right in.

00:18:39.167 --> 00:18:42.542
Of course. Let's do it.

00:18:43.417 --> 00:18:43.875
He threatens dismissal and concocts a gamble

00:18:43.875 --> 00:18:45.333
"Tentacle"
He threatens dismissal and concocts a gamble

00:18:45.333 --> 00:18:48.292
"Tentacle"
that's clearly in his favor.

00:18:48.292 --> 00:18:51.875
"Tentacle"
But there's no backing down.

00:18:51.875 --> 00:18:57.042
Mathematically, it has better odds
than any of our other attempts.

00:18:57.042 --> 00:19:00.333
To be one of the strong--
<i>that's </i>the mightiest blade.

00:19:00.333 --> 00:19:03.625
Truly, the principal's assassination!

00:19:03.625 --> 00:19:08.917
Open and solve, then close--
do it all at once and it won't explode.

00:19:08.917 --> 00:19:12.083
With your speed, it may even be easy.

00:19:12.083 --> 00:19:14.750
Y-Yes, of co--of course!

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.708
"Geometry II"

00:19:33.625 --> 00:19:34.875
Planar calculations!

00:19:34.875 --> 00:19:38.083
Um, well, that's an easy one--
it's, you know, that thing,

00:19:38.083 --> 00:19:41.375
where you borrow from the tens
to get 3 with 4 left over,

00:19:41.375 --> 00:19:44.042
or, say, about 3 or so--

00:19:47.333 --> 00:19:49.708
Just like with that metal ring puzzle,

00:19:49.708 --> 00:19:53.292
I know how your reaction-and thinking
speed drop when you're flustered.

00:19:53.292 --> 00:19:57.083
You can't get past this trap.

00:19:57.083 --> 00:19:59.208
Koro Sensei...

00:19:59.208 --> 00:20:04.167
First one is a hit. Make it through
three more and you win.

00:20:04.167 --> 00:20:09.042
"Notice of Dismissal"
Now solve the next, before you recover.

00:20:09.042 --> 00:20:12.833
You're kiddin' me!
He can't take three more of those!

00:20:12.833 --> 00:20:16.833
Is he really gonna get taken down
by such a simple setup?

00:20:16.833 --> 00:20:20.708
The weak can only kill
the strong through assassination,

00:20:20.708 --> 00:20:25.167
but the strong can kill the weak
whenever and however they like.

00:20:25.167 --> 00:20:30.167
I will pepper the nation
with mechanisms to teach this truth.

00:20:30.167 --> 00:20:34.250
With my money from the Ministry of Defense
and the bounty from killing you,

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:37.500
I can build my affiliate schools
all over the country.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.333
It's <i>always </i>about education with him.

00:20:40.333 --> 00:20:43.458
"Training"
"Social Studies" "History"

00:20:43.458 --> 00:20:46.417
Now, Koro Sensei...

00:20:46.417 --> 00:20:50.417
...be the cornerstone of my philosophy.

00:21:03.375 --> 00:21:08.875
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:08.875 --> 00:21:14.250
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:19.958
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:19.958 --> 00:21:25.083
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:21:25.083 --> 00:21:36.458
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:21:36.458 --> 00:21:42.042
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:21:42.042 --> 00:21:46.458
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:21:46.458 --> 00:21:53.292
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:21:53.292 --> 00:21:58.792
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:21:58.792 --> 00:22:04.292
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:04.292 --> 00:22:11.625
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>

00:22:23.167 --> 00:22:23.583
Surprise!

00:22:23.583 --> 00:22:24.208
"Tell Us, Kunudon!"
Surprise!

00:22:24.208 --> 00:22:27.208
"Tell Us, Kunudon!"
Tell us, Kunudon!

00:22:27.208 --> 00:22:30.458
Phew! That school festival
was a real white-knuckler,

00:22:30.458 --> 00:22:33.917
but it looks like the E Class
is finally down for the count!

00:22:33.917 --> 00:22:36.792
Show's over!

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:40.083
Nah-nah! Riffraff! Garbage!

00:22:40.083 --> 00:22:42.583
Serves you right!

00:22:45.083 --> 00:22:46.500
Oh!

00:22:46.875 --> 00:22:51.042
Mr. Principal, sir, what brings you here?

00:22:51.042 --> 00:22:53.667
"Notice of Dismissal: Kunudon"
Notice of dismissal!

00:22:53.667 --> 00:22:56.792
I'm... going to the E Class?!

00:22:56.792 --> 00:23:02.102
Reemployment refugee! Yay!
